    <node id="Strong Demand">
      <data key="d0">Strong Demand</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Strong Demand, in the context of global energy markets, refers to a high level of consumer, industrial, and overall market interest in petroleum products, most notably crude oil. This economic condition is consistently identified as a key fundamental factor that supports, contributes to, and drives the rally, rise, and sustained increase in crude oil prices. The relationship is defined by the principle that strong demand for oil directly supports upward price movements, acting as a primary driver behind the sustained price increases observed in the market.

Specifically, strong demand for oil is a factor supporting the rally in crude oil prices, contributing to higher crude oil prices and supporting crude oil price increases. It is consistently described as a factor that supports the rally in crude oil prices, contributing to the overall upward trend in the market. Strong demand refers to high consumer or industrial demand for oil, which contributed to rising crude oil prices.</data>
