    <node id="Safe-Haven Assets">
      <data key="d0">Safe-Haven Assets</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Safe-Haven Assets are financial instruments or commodities that investors seek out during periods of market uncertainty, downturns, or selloffs in order to preserve value and manage risk. The most prominent example of a safe-haven asset is gold, which consistently attracts investor interest when economic conditions become volatile or unstable. This behavior is observable in market data, such as the rise in gold futures during turbulent times. The primary function of these assets is to act as a store of value, providing a hedge against risk and capital preservation when other investments, such as equities, are declining.

Investors turn to safe-haven assets like gold specifically during market downturns and periods of uncertainty to protect their capital. The consistent pattern of gold attracting investment during such volatile periods underscores its role as a reliable store of value and a defensive strategy against broader market selloffs. As a risk management strategy, these assets are sought by investors to safeguard their portfolios when broader economic conditions become unstable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89db22b0e5a6074ecc3ea2ba20783879&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ba10301a1cc50aa00b42c346bc0be73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6a85b577f748f823a732efe5f33bcc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c4426fe3d656d20408ebd50181707d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0253c8fd4cf1a734f1e20c69452e83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6218739cb192cff96f29ab446f3c5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-990274235a3a49eed4cdcbefe01ab063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba9e539e2a95244b725131333cf02b15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d9d0f08c60fc1566be4d59b80e3ce8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-781a874dfa08b29a9052bcfdfde2061b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee4e0bc4d3f900c9271fab93b63caf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b606597aae507436e4bc3368049cab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e827ebe778b4fe39c952a40be61f9bc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8d08b51b94e473897b7e18847e55ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-450f069284fc5692d5ade6bb4aeb0deb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-654210e4a83c095d604993852216dccb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e66405bf753e63b7b1c564dd5e86db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58b70a42920a91dffdca8121d66a66eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c0c72057a06111028608a0973aef2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be25df1af7e30c6a7392305cb22b52d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb1ce8466eba9fca5a2139cfe96ff1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f944c8f4f3100f826c0cf74b0febe515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecd4725f61a32f7fdf146cfa86e9ffbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-296a72753256021351c386543f50f98c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3886638a85ee14393d1da2d826028ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68fc75e0518c7a7c27f8e04edf36f2d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89b412cfc15b061e0a7f50978f8d7142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48c5edb800b10683bdc0233af08cf3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b79bbc9970c9b816e5baf5ef4c75ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7a7e69bbfc6d988c3b624dbb865e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146af96f6ee6ac7b66eefff49c0f3756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89799248c4126aacb846167b35f83e6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f1a8aae31051ab5ad1792bad2f9b4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a409f0c18103033f1c4f6387ed11cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99b50c91999c3bd07c0062342808aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62cb7ea60b6bc057b91edb59c37463f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24d2a0eeb5394c1bb2920dce48699105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a8e0964a7d0c184c2475b3e18aba43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7c33a304af0ab2f99ea0a8298e156a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-514d21a96f5f1