      <data key="d2">The relation (Investor Concerns, Market Selloff) describes a causal link where investor anxiety directly triggers a broad decline in asset prices. The primary drivers of these concerns are rising interest rates and regulatory uncertainty. These two factors are consistently identified as the root cause, with descriptions using terms such as "primary cause," "directly caused," "causing," and "triggered" to establish the connection. The selloff is presented as an ongoing or recent event, with the relationship being described in both present and past tense across the provided descriptions.</data>
