    <node id="Computer Communication Technology">
      <data key="d0">Computer Communication Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Computer Communication Technology is the organic integration of computer and communication technologies, focusing on computer communication network technology and multimedia communication technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computer Communication Network Technology">
      <data key="d0">Computer Communication Network Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Computer Communication Network Technology expands the scope of information transmission, especially through wireless communication, enabling network systems in hard-to-reach areas and relying on TCP/IP protocol for global interconnectivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Multimedia Communication Technology">
      <data key="d0">Multimedia Communication Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Multimedia Communication Technology uses multimedia forms for information transmission, with computers as the control core, enabling the collection, processing, storage, and transmission of multimedia information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Codec Technology">
      <data key="d0">Codec Technology</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Codec Technology is the core of network multimedia communication technology, compressing and decompressing data to enable the transmission of massive multimedia information over limited bandwidth, with mainstream standards including MPEG, H.264/265, and AVS.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Information System">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Information System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Electronic Information System is a human-machine integrated system composed of computer hardware, network and communication equipment, software, information resources, users, and regulations, with functions of input, storage, processing, output, and control of information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="National Defense Command Information System">
      <data key="d0">National Defense Command Information System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">National Defense Command Information System, also known as the comprehensive electronic information system, is a military information system integrating command, control, communication, computer, intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance for military information acquisition, processing, decision support, and battlefield management.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Defense Command Information System is a field where the company develops products to meet the special needs of military command networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad50c45c4371d5107a8c28dd3c832fd9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780278564</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TCP/IP Protocol">
      <data key="d0">TCP/IP Protocol</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">TCP/IP Protocol is a key protocol enabling global interconnectivity across different hardware structures, operating systems, and network systems in computer communication networks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="H.264/265">
      <data key="d0">H.264/265</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">H.264/265 are mainstream codec technology standards used in network multimedia communication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="C4ISR System">
      <data key="d0">C4ISR System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">C4ISR System is the US military term for the National Defense Command Information System, encompassing Command, Control, Communication, Computer, Intelligence, Surveillance, and Reconnaissance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1780276284</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd.">
      <data key="d0">Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd.</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd. is the company that issued the prospectus from which the provided text is extracted, and it serves as the subject of the associated accounting policies and financial data analysis. The company reported financial information including prepayments, other receivables, and related transactions. It is also the owner of a portfolio of trademarks.

The company develops video fusion platforms and related products, serving sectors such as the military, prisons, and oil fields. Its manufacturing operations involve the production of customized codecs and servers, which are created through software recording and modular assembly processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14d4e7213768e5a9d7a66bec241ce01e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-524e4292263105f9427d5413618e9c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-715426c8536b679514108da2caab6b17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32adcca902f2d818c44b9e6713cc9db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad50c45c4371d5107a8c28dd3c832fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-978f7aa25dfd256e7ee6730f7852f7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67a0e15a163891dc3165e7d1e9a9c5cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51aa5d05f6f437fca7d5c1043da8ff1</data>
