      <data key="d0">应付票据</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Notes payable, a current liability item on the balance sheet, with amounts listed for various dates.&lt;SEP&gt;应付票据is a financial data item representing notes payable, with values reported for multiple periods.&lt;SEP&gt;应付票据是公司应付的票据，原单独列报，后与应付账款合并。&lt;SEP&gt;应付票据是公司财务报表中的项目，涉及会计政策变更和金额调整。&lt;SEP&gt;应付票据is a notes payable component of current liabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;应付票据refers to notes payable, including bank acceptance bills of 385.30 and 174.66 (in 10,000 yuan) due in June 2019 and November 2019, respectively, for supplier payments.</data>
