    <node id="应付账款">
      <data key="d0">应付账款</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Accounts payable, a current liability item on the balance sheet, with amounts listed for various dates.&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款is a financial data item representing accounts payable, with values reported for multiple periods.&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款是公司应付的款项，原单独列报，后与应付票据合并。&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款是公司财务报表中的项目，涉及会计政策变更和金额调整。&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款is a balance sheet item representing accounts payable, with adjusted amounts of 15,334,822.58元in 2019 and 19,806,932.97元in 2016.&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款is an accounting concept representing accounts payable.&lt;SEP&gt;应付账款refers to accounts payable, primarily for supplier payments, with balances of 1,980.69, 2,137.04, 1,684.62, and 1,533.48 (in 10,000 yuan) at the end of each reporting period.</data>
