    <edge source="Investor Concerns" target="Regulatory Uncertainty">
      <data key="d7">161.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation (Investor Concerns, Regulatory Uncertainty) describes a causal and contributory link in which regulatory uncertainty acts as a significant factor that amplifies or drives investor concerns. Across multiple descriptions, regulatory uncertainty is consistently identified as a key, primary, or contributing component of investor concerns. This uncertainty is not only a general source of worry but is also specifically cited as a driving force behind market selloffs and a contributor to broader market instability. The relationship is framed as both a present and past dynamic, indicating that regulatory uncertainty has been and continues to be a persistent element that heightens investor anxiety and negatively influences market conditions.

Regulatory uncertainty adds to investor concerns and market volatility, influencing market behavior and contributing to concerns about market stability. It is a key factor fueling investor concerns and is a primary source and cause of those concerns. Regulatory uncertainty contributes to investor concerns and market instability, and it is a concern for investors contributing to the selloff. Overall, regulatory uncertainty is a persistent and significant driver of investor concerns, affecting market conditions and stability.</data>
      <data key="d9">anxiety,causal factor,causation,cause and effect,economic factor,investor sentiment,market anxiety,market driver,market impact,market risk,market sentiment,market volatility,policy factor,policy impact,policy risk,regulatory environment,regulatory factor,regulatory impact</data>
