    <edge source="Federal Reserve" target="Market Selloff">
      <data key="d7">25.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between the Federal Reserve and a market selloff is characterized by the influence of the central bank's policy actions and communications on investor behavior and market stability. Speculation over the Federal Reserve's policy announcement, particularly regarding potential rate hikes, contributed to market volatility and directly influenced the investor selloff. This speculation, rather than a confirmed policy change, was a key driver of the market downturn, as uncertainty over the Fed's future direction eroded investor confidence.

The Federal Reserve's upcoming policy announcement was expected to be a critical event, with its outcome likely to either stabilize or further destabilize the market. Overall, the market selloff was not triggered by a single event but was the result of heightened sensitivity to anticipated Federal Reserve policy changes, which created an environment of volatility and prompted investors to sell off assets. The Federal Reserve's policy decisions are expected to influence investor confidence and overall market stability.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Reserve's policy decisions are expected to influence investor confidence and market stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over the Federal Reserve's potential rate hikes contributed to market volatility and the investor selloff.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over the Federal Reserve's policy decisions is influencing the market selloff.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over Federal Reserve policy changes contributed to market volatility and investor selloff.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over Federal Reserve policy changes is influencing investor confidence and contributing to the market selloff.</data>
      <data key="d9">financial regulation,influence,interest rate impact,market impact,market influence,market stability,monetary policy,policy impact,policy influence</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8455459f679507928ed432ed0eeb11a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8073427e62e9928dc9d4d2e1bf551bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-560cb7117e9d5c8fe2ebe3fce7fe2b14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bba9eac029b302aabf1571d3c8bb5ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a439299f90cd269df576a65e3aec0bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395c544cbdbc0fb5c7f956be865084b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3104b9748246bf1c1b596137af31103a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f59a37440ab95ef90b5519bda697b22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abd183f52aef118cb63810c498ab8550&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e6ef010bba2a819545e29f981f9a6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb09edb1098f9d43c10eb37e8eaf03aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca02fbab0d237ce11800b5b73d4efd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66bf9577dcccaac7aa541c5650962f89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8fc31188e449d6106dadda0587623f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14aa9b61d5d5a1090625ae2c5607e5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85051b285f1c500763f83db7eb74a280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af143b0c95988c6fbd428d9191ea6fe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c51aa5d05f6f437fca7d5c1043da8ff1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93fb79958d661926096c59442d227d57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ad4c2dae4e12654bb3e81ead3541cb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-735c1e7025b476d06d2968a85d58fc1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf933ea6ad543d32c5edbe9d972ca701&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63e5d2afa2bb086b998b098937fd536f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f75cc135f18da22cc4087015b843cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af88a45916f0db4a042242b4f213402</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1780280486</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Federal Reserve" target="Federal Reserve Policy Announcement">
      <data key="d7">28.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The Federal Reserve is responsible for its upcoming policy announcement, which is expected to influence both investor confidence and overall market stability. This announcement is consistently described as a key event that will have a significant impact on market conditions, affecting the stability of financial markets and the sentiment of investors. The Federal Reserve's role in this process underscores its authority in shaping economic expectations through its policy communications. The announcement is anticipated to be a primary factor in determining the direction of market stability and investor confidence, highlighting the central bank's influence on the broader economic landscape.</data>
      <data key="d9">causation,central bank action,central banking,decision-making,interest rates,market impact,market influence,monetary policy,organizational action,policy,policy action,policy decision,policy impact,policy making</data>
