    <edge source="Market Stability" target="Federal Reserve Policy Announcement">
      <data key="d7">94.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation (Federal Reserve Policy Announcement, Market Stability) describes the anticipated effect of a formal statement from the central bank of the United States on the condition of financial markets. The Federal Reserve's policy announcement, whether upcoming or general, is expected to influence overall market stability. This influence is consistently characterized as an impact on the broad, systemic steadiness of financial markets, with the announcement serving as a key driver of market conditions. The descriptions emphasize that the announcement is a primary factor expected to affect the equilibrium and predictability of the financial system.

