    <edge source="Lower-Than-Expected Quarterly Earnings" target="Nexon Technologies">
      <data key="d7">45.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation (Lower-Than-Expected Quarterly Earnings, Nexon Technologies) describes a direct causal financial event in which Nexon Technologies reported quarterly earnings that fell below market expectations. This disappointing financial performance is consistently identified as the primary and sole driver of a subsequent negative market reaction, leading to a decline in the company's stock price. The relationship is characterized as a direct and immediate causal link, with the earnings miss being the only attributed cause for the stock's downturn.

The impact of this earnings miss was quantified, with the stock experiencing a specific decline of 7.8%. Multiple descriptions reinforce that the stock "plummeted" as a direct result of the lower-than-expected earnings, with no other contributing factors mentioned. The event is uniformly described across all provided descriptions as a straightforward cause-and-effect relationship: the lower-than-expected quarterly earnings directly caused Nexon Technologies' stock to decline.&lt;SEP&gt;Nexon Technologies' lower-than-expected quarterly earnings caused its stock to plummet.&lt;SEP&gt;Nexon Technologies' stock decline was directly caused by its lower-than-expected quarterly earnings.&lt;SEP&gt;Nexon Technologies reported lower-than-expected quarterly earnings, causing its stock to plummet.&lt;SEP&gt;Nexon Technologies' lower-than-expected quarterly earnings caused its stock to plummet by 7.8%.</data>
      <data key="d9">causation,company performance,corporate event,corporate performance,earnings report,financial event,financial performance,financial reporting,financial result,financial results,stock impact</data>
