    <edge source="Safe-Haven Assets" target="Gold Futures">
      <data key="d7">63.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation between Gold Futures and Safe-Haven Assets describes a well-established financial dynamic in which gold futures are consistently categorized and classified as a type of safe-haven asset. During periods of market uncertainty, such as a selloff or broader economic downturn, investors actively seek out these assets to protect their capital. This behavior results in a rise in the price of gold futures, as increased demand from investors drives the market upward.

The relationship is consistently observed across various market conditions, including selloffs and broader downturns, reinforcing the role of gold futures as a preferred refuge during times of financial instability. Multiple observations confirm that gold futures rise as investors seek safe-haven assets during market selloffs, highlighting the consistent and predictable nature of this relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold futures rose as investors sought safe-haven assets during the market selloff.&lt;SEP&gt;Gold futures rose as investors sought safe-haven assets during the market selloff.</data>
