    <edge source="Speculation Over Rate Hikes" target="Federal Reserve Policy Announcement">
      <data key="d7">13.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation "Federal Reserve Policy Announcement, Speculation Over Rate Hikes" describes a dynamic where market and public speculation regarding potential increases in interest rates is directly connected to the Federal Reserve's forthcoming policy announcement. This speculation is actively influencing expectations and growing in intensity as the announcement approaches. The speculation is consistently characterized as being linked to, tied to, or influencing the expectations surrounding the upcoming policy decision.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over potential rate hikes is linked to the upcoming Federal Reserve policy announcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over potential rate hikes is linked to the upcoming Federal Reserve policy announcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over potential rate hikes is linked to the upcoming Federal Reserve policy announcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Speculation over potential rate hikes is centered on the Federal Reserve's upcoming policy announcement.</data>
      <data key="d9">anticipation,causation,market anticipation,market expectation,market influence,market speculation,policy anticipation,policy impact</data>
